{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790990240,"nonce":"DcHRrtvFodJ8SgXclf4SfVK8gGc=","message":"Landed in 2752833.\n\nParsing: haxe/ashui/svg reads Haxe Xml into SvgDocument: shapes (path, rect, circle, ellipse, line, polyline, polygon) as absolute PathCommands; groups with opacity and transform; solid and currentColor paint; inherited fill and stroke properties; style declarations. Errors are SvgError. The hxx macro turns an inline \u003csvg\u003e into Xml and parses it at compile time, and so do SvgDocument.of(\u003csvg\u003e...\u003c/svg\u003e) (Haxe inline markup) and SvgDocument.embed(path). Documents are interned by their canonical markup.\n\nDrawing: blinc_abi gives a node an image slot and the paint walk emits a PRIM_IMAGE record in paint order. Haxe (core/render/Images) rasterizes each document at its bucketed on-screen size through blinc_svg, packs it into an RGBA ImageAtlas (shelves, uploads by region, growth by GPU copy), and ImageShader draws it: a currentColor-only document is a mask tinted with the element's colour, anything else is drawn as written.\n\nCrossing to Blinc as canonical markup rather than raw path arrays keeps the binding to blinc_svg's existing entry point, and the markup is only what the parser already checked.\n\nNot yet: gradients, \u003cuse\u003e/\u003cdefs\u003e, \u003ctext\u003e, clip paths and masks (all reported as unsupported); colour that passes from a parent element (CSS currentColor inheritance), which needs a decision on inheritance in ashui generally; releasing documents parsed at runtime (they stay in the registry).","files":null}]}